<h3>C. Hinglish sentiment (RQ1)</h3>
<p class="ni">{{ tref('hing') }} and {{ fref('lang') }} compare single-task MuRIL with single-task HingRoBERTa, with the same splits, hyperparameters, and seeds. HingRoBERTa selected itself on validation, where its Hinglish gain was {{ dci(STS,HING,'val','sentiment','macro_f1','language:hi-Latn') }}. On test it improves Hinglish macro-F1 from {{ m(STS,'sentiment','macro_f1','language:hi-Latn') }} to {{ m(HING,'sentiment','macro_f1','language:hi-Latn') }}, a difference of {{ dci(STS,HING,'test','sentiment','macro_f1','language:hi-Latn') }}, and the gain appears on both Hinglish sources. English changes by {{ dci(STS,HING,'test','sentiment','macro_f1','language:en-Latn') }}, so we cannot claim an English effect in either direction. The English to Hinglish gap falls from {{ '%.3f' % (m(STS,'sentiment','macro_f1','language:en-Latn')|float - m(STS,'sentiment','macro_f1','language:hi-Latn')|float) }} to {{ '%.3f' % (m(HING,'sentiment','macro_f1','language:en-Latn')|float - m(HING,'sentiment','macro_f1','language:hi-Latn')|float) }}, a reduction of {{ '%.0f' % (100*(1 - (m(HING,'sentiment','macro_f1','language:en-Latn')|float - m(HING,'sentiment','macro_f1','language:hi-Latn')|float)/(m(STS,'sentiment','macro_f1','language:en-Latn')|float - m(STS,'sentiment','macro_f1','language:hi-Latn')|float))) }}%.</p>
