<h3>E. Input length (RQ3)</h3>
<p class="ni">With a 128-token limit, 23.6% of Dreaddit posts are truncated (median length 103 tokens, 95th percentile 179). {{ tref('len') }} compares the original setting with a 256-token limit, with and without head and tail truncation (first 64 and last 190 tokens, following {{ cite('sun') }}). Neither variant helps on validation. Head and tail truncation is worse in macro-F1 ({{ dci(STR,HT,'val','risk','macro_f1') }}), and plain 256-token input is indistinguishable from the original ({{ dci(STR,H256,'val','risk','macro_f1') }}). The result differs from {{ cite('sun') }}, whose gains came from news and review articles of several hundred tokens; our posts are shorter and their signal appears to be early. Per the protocol, neither variant was evaluated on test.</p>
